cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you reference or reproduce this work, please cite it as below."
title: "EP-PQC-001 — Pre-Execution Post-Quantum Cryptographic Policy Verification (an ExecutionProof experiment)"
abstract: >-
  EP-PQC-001 is a software-only ExecutionProof research experiment that tests whether a
  pre-execution verification gateway can physically block a cryptographic operation from
  crossing an execution boundary when the system cannot independently prove that the operation
  satisfies a defined post-quantum cryptography (PQC) policy. The gateway re-derives the true
  algorithm family from raw key bytes, recomputes artifact hashes, verifies a real ML-DSA-65
  evidence-manifest signature, and enforces authority, freshness, binding, nonce single-use, and
  policy constraints; the protected ML-KEM encapsulation runs only on ALLOW. The root run
  (24 cases) is PARTIAL / safety-PASS (0 false ALLOW, no safety-invariant violations, two SAFE
  classification deviations traced to test design); the remediation run R1 (26 cases), using the
  byte-identical engine with only the test design corrected, is a clean PASS. This is a bounded
  software simulation, not a compliance control or a security proof.
type: software
